<h1>balanced merge sort</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A <a href="kwayMergeSort.html"><em>k-way merge sort</em></a> in which the number of input and  output data streams is the same.  See <a href="balanckwayms.html"><em>balanced k-way merge sort</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="mergesort.html"><em>merge sort</em></a>, <a href="simplemerge.html"><em>simple merge</em></a>, <a href="nonbalncmsrt.html"><em>nonbalanced merge sort</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
This is an <a href="externalsort.html"><em>external sort</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorASK">ASK</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/4/442.sort.c" target="_blank">(C)</a> using an auxiliary function to <a href="https://users.dcc.uchile.cl/~rbaeza/handbook/algs/4/442.next.c" target="_blank">select next file (C)</a>.

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

